/-!
# The natural single-factor Baumann theorem

For the actual natural SL₂ quotient supplied by B.6.9, the source Sylow
and alpha conclusions are proved with the original centralizer kernel.
The companion endpoint retains the literal moved subgroup [U,O²(H)] and
its natural quotient, giving B.6.10(3) exactly. All Thompson-image,
residual-generation, fixed-dimension and Frattini inputs are discharged.
The multiple-factor reduction and production of the natural marker are
separate source classification steps; no conclusion is encoded as input.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith B.6.10 and E.2.3, pp.117 and216–217.
-/
